            "review_title": "Review at Bep Thin - Thin Kitchen",
            "review_text": "BaoPhan\nDa Nang, Vietnam29 contributions\n0\nTasty and addicted Vietnamese food, unique decor style. Everything I need is here\nFeb 2019 • Couples\nBeen looking for a new dinner experience for a while and suddenly stop at this little Indochine style restaurant. Nice decor, the old paintings are nice and reflect exactly the same atmosphere as if we are back in time.\nMostly common Vietnamese traditional dishes like white rice, fish in claypot, caramelized pork and eggs, pork, hotpot, pork saute, shrimp... It tasted amazingly good. Despite I have Vietnamese food everyday, these dishes brought something very unique. The taste is different, and super nice.\nThe hotpot is a plus too, sour and spicy with fish, my favourite one.\nAt night we get a view to Dragon Bridge and out in balcony, very windy and comfortable space. Highly recommended for a romantic dinner.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 10, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
